title: "06b  Competitive bidding under the New Government Procurement Act (RA 12009): who does what, with the time limits"
---
sequenceDiagram
  autonumber
  %% QUESTION THIS DIAGRAM ANSWERS: from the request of the end-user to the notice to proceed, which body acts at each step, and how long may each step take?
  %% SOURCES: every step and time limit below is from Republic Act No. 12009 as published on lawphil.net [RA12009]: pre-procurement conference s.49, pre-bid conference s.51, opening of bids s.58, ceiling on bids s.60, evaluation s.61, post-qualification s.63, award, contract and notice to proceed s.66, 60-day limit s.67, performance security s.68, observers s.43, protest ss.83-87, early procurement s.12, PhilGEPS s.20.
  %% THE IMPLEMENTING RULES (GPPB Resolution No. 02-2025, in effect since 25 February 2025) add details that I did not open [GPPB-ADV]. Where the Act and the Rules differ in a number of days, the Rules decide the practice.
  %% GENERAL KNOWLEDGE, NOT OPENED IN A SOURCE HERE: the names of the notices (Invitation to Bid, Notice of Award, Notice to Proceed) and the BAC resolution in step 13, the question and answer in steps 2 and 3 (the Act requires the certification, it does not describe who asks whom).
  participant EU as End-user<br/>unit
  participant BAC as Bids and Awards Committee (BAC)<br/>with Secretariat and working group
  participant FIN as Budget and<br/>accounting units
  participant HOPE as Head of the<br/>procuring entity
  participant PG as PhilGEPS<br/>(electronic portal)
  participant BID as Bidders
  participant OBS as Observers<br/>(private sector, civil society)
  participant COA as COA

  EU->>BAC: Purchase request, specifications, bidding documents<br/>for an item in the Annual Procurement Plan
  BAC->>FIN: Is the funding available?
  FIN-->>BAC: Certification of availability of funds
  BAC->>BAC: Pre-procurement conference: confirm readiness<br/>#nbsp;
  BAC->>PG: Publish the invitation to bid and the bidding documents
  PG-->>BID: Notice visible to registered suppliers
  BAC->>BID: Pre-bid conference, at least 12 days<br/>before the deadline for bids
  BID->>BAC: Bids: eligibility documents, technical bid, financial bid
  BAC->>OBS: Invitation to observe each stage
  BAC->>BAC: Eligibility screening. Opening of bids within<br/>1 day after the deadline. A bid above the<br/>approved budget for the contract is disqualified<br/>#nbsp;
  BAC->>BAC: Bid evaluation within 7 days. Rank by the award criterion<br/>#nbsp;
  loop Until one bidder passes, starting from the first in rank
    BAC->>BID: Post-qualification within 12 days:<br/>verify documents and capacity of the bidder
  end
  BAC->>HOPE: Resolution recommending award
  HOPE-->>BID: Notice of award, within 10 days<br/>from the recommendation
  HOPE->>PG: Award published
  BID->>HOPE: Performance security, before signing
  HOPE->>BID: Contract signed within 10 days from the notice of award
  HOPE->>BID: Notice to proceed within 3 days<br/>from approval of the contract
  OBS-->>HOPE: Observation report (copies to PhilGEPS and COA)
  OBS-->>COA: Observation report

  Note over BAC,BID: TOTAL TIME: from opening of bids to award, not more than 60 days.<br/>AWARD CRITERIA: lowest calculated responsive bid (goods, works), most economically advantageous<br/>responsive bid (quality and price), highest rated responsive bid (consulting services).
  Note over EU,HOPE: EARLY PROCUREMENT: all steps up to the recommendation may be done before the GAA,<br/>but no award may be made until the funding is approved and effective.
  opt A losing bidder objects
    BID->>BAC: Request for reconsideration
    BID->>HOPE: Protest through the electronic system, with a fee.<br/>After that, review by the Regional Trial Court
  end
